<Prose title="OpenClaw on Sabha — Open Source AI Assistant for Communities" description="Run an AI assistant — OpenAI, Anthropic, or local LLMs — inside Sabha rooms and DMs. Open source, self-hosted, no webhook URL needed." label="INTEGRATION" heading="OpenClaw on Sabha">
  <img slot="mark" src="/_site/logos/openclaw-claw.svg" alt="OpenClaw" width="56" height="56" />
  <FeatureVideo slot="figure" name="bot" width={1280} height={720} label="An OpenClaw AI agent in a Sabha room" />
  <p>Sabha provides first-class <a href="https://openclaw.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="landing-link">OpenClaw</a> support over WebSockets. The AI bot connects outbound to your workspace — no webhook URL to configure, no public IP to expose, no tunnels. OpenClaw works with self-hosted Sabha, multi-tenant SaaS mode on sabha.co, and dedicated instances managed by Sabha Cloud Deploy.</p>

  <p>@mention it in any room, or DM it directly, and it replies — powered by the LLM of your choice (OpenAI, Anthropic, or a local model).</p>

  <p>No third-party chat dependency, no third-party AI dependency. OpenClaw runs on Discord, Telegram, Slack, and a dozen other channels — but with Sabha you can self-host the entire stack. Your community, your bot, your data, your servers.</p>

  <h3>How it works</h3>

  <ol>
    <li>Add Sabha to OpenClaw: <code>openclaw plugins install @sabha-co/openclaw-sabha</code></li>
    <li>Run <code>openclaw configure --section channels</code> and paste a Sabha join URL.</li>
    <li>@mention the bot in any room, or DM it directly. It's that quiet.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>What the AI can do</h3>

  <p>Rooms, threads, DMs, reactions, attachments, search — the AI speaks Sabha natively. Give it MCP tools, RAG over your community's docs, vision on uploaded images, voice — anything OpenClaw skills support. In rooms it only replies when @mentioned, so it stays out of the way. In DMs it's always listening.</p>

  <h3>Get started</h3>

